Ladybird walks the containing blocks of a wheel target until it finds
an ancestor with a compositor scroll node. Blink walks containing
boxes in ScrollManager::RecomputeScrollChain and scroll nodes in
cc::InputHandler::FindNodeToLatch. Gecko builds a chain to the
scrollable ancestor in APZCTreeManager::BuildOverscrollHandoffChain.
WebKit checks the enclosing scrollable areas through EventHandler and
ScrollLatchingController::shouldLatchToScrollableArea.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 all scrolled the
page under the fixed clipping box. A visible scrollable panel took
the wheel itself. A transformed outer scroller took the step when it
established the fixed overlay’s containing block.
